rt( (2 l g \\tan \\alpha)^2 + 4 l^2 g^2 ) ] / 2\n\nSimplify discriminant:\n\n(2 l g \\tan \\alpha)^2 + 4 l^2 g^2 = 4 l^2 g^2 \\tan^2 \\alpha + 4 l^2 g^2 = 4 l^2 g^2 (tan^2 \\alpha + 1) = 4 l^2 g^2 sec^2 \\alpha\n\nThus:\n\nu = [ -2 l g \\tan \\alpha \u00b1 2 l g \\sec \\alpha ] / 2 = [ -l g \\tan \\alpha \u00b1 l g \\sec \\alpha ]\n\nSince u = v_1^2 must be positive, take the positive root:\n\nu = l g ( - tan \\alpha + sec \\alpha ) = l g ( \\sec \\alpha - \\tan \\alpha )\n\nTherefore,\n\nv_1^2 = l g ( \\sec \\alpha - \\tan \\alpha ) = l g \\left( \\frac{1}{\\cos \\alpha} - \\frac{\\sin \\alpha}{\\cos \\alpha} \\right ) = l g \\frac{1 - \\sin \\alpha}{\\cos \\alpha }\n\nWhich matches the expression given in the problem statement. Therefore, the error was in the original problem statement where the safety parabola equation was missing a square on \\( v_1 \\). With this correction, the derivation works out.\n\nNow, using conservation of energy to find \\( v_0 \\). The stone is thrown from the ground with speed \\( v_0 \\), reaches the top of the building with speed \\( v_1 \\), and height \\( H \\). The conservation of energy gives:\n\n\\( \\frac{1}{2} m v_0^2 = \\frac{1}{2} m v_1^2 + m g H \\)\n\nSimplifying:\n\n\\( v_0^2 = v_1^2 + 2 g H \\)\n\nSubstituting \\( v_1^2 = g l \\frac{1 - \\sin \\alpha}{\\cos \\alpha} \\):\n\n\\( v_0^2 = g l \\frac{1 - \\sin \\alpha}{\\cos \\alpha} + 2 g H \\)\n\nFactor out \\( g \\):\n\n\\( v_0^2 = g \\left( 2 H + l \\frac{1 - \\sin \\alpha}{\\cos \\alpha} \\right ) \\)\n\nTherefore, the minimum speed is:\n\n\\( v_0 = \\sqrt{ g \\left( 2 H + l \\frac{1 - \\sin \\alpha}{\\cos \\alpha} \\right ) } \\)\n\nThis matches the expression given in the problem statement. So the key steps were:\n\n1. Correct the safety parabola equation to have \\( v_1^2 \\) in the first term.\n2. Substitute the coordinates of the lower corner into the corrected equation.\n3. Solve the resulting quadratic in \\( v_1^2 \\).\n4. Use energy conservation to relate \\( 